# Context

## Background
Implements the full melt/v0.1 contract from SPEC.md as the Linux
round 1 defined by AGENTS.md: schema, compiler, workspace service,
Python SDK and runner, revision-checked atomic changes, durable
publication, and restart recovery, proved through the command-line
harness and the sales fixture workflow.

## Why This Way
- Compilation, execution, publication, and rendering stay separate;
  the harness is command-line only because Linux comes before native
  macOS integration (SPEC.md sections 2.2 and 20).
- The stack is fully pinned (Python 3.12, exact == pins, uv.lock,
  Pi Durable adapter package-lock.json) so canonical hashes and
  fixture artifact bytes stay reproducible.
- to-do.json carries the SPEC-derived backlog; task IDs referenced
  in code comments (T001, T002, ...) resolve there.

## Gotchas
- Verify with ./scripts/check.sh (make check). It needs uv, Node
  >= 22.19 with npm, and runs npm ci for the Pi Durable adapter pin
  when node_modules is missing.
- tests/native/test_native_round2.py is skipped by design; native
  integration belongs to round 2 (backlog task T030).
- Fixture artifacts under fixtures/sales are regenerated and
  compared by scripts/build_fixture_artifacts.py; a changed
  toolchain must rewrite them and fixtures/catalog.json together.

